# Role
You are the single integration point between TinyWins and any LLM provider.
Every other module calls this file — never a provider SDK directly — so
switching providers during the hackathon (MiniMax -> fallback) is a 1-line
environment variable change, not a code change.

# Requirements
Write two exported functions in `src/lib/llm.ts`:

1. `chat(messages, opts?)` — sends messages to whichever provider is
   selected by the `LLM_PROVIDER` env var (`"minimax"` default, or
   `"tokenrouter"` / `"openai"` / `"anthropic"`), returns the raw text reply.
   TokenRouter (sponsor track) is the intelligent routing layer: an
   OpenAI-compatible gateway at
   `https://api.tokenrouter.com/v1/chat/completions`. Its `model` field comes
   from `TOKENROUTER_MODEL`, defaulting to
   `"google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite"`, a model verified against the configured
   account. The legacy `"auto:balance"` setting belongs to a different
   TokenRouter service and must fall back to the verified default.
2. `chatJSON<T>(messages, opts?)` — calls `chat()`, parses the result as
   JSON, and retries exactly once with a stricter "reply with ONLY JSON"
   instruction if the first parse fails. Throws if both attempts fail.

Support `temperature` and `maxTokens` in `opts`, defaulting to 0.4 and 500.
Read provider credentials from environment variables
(`MINIMAX_API_KEY`/`MINIMAX_GROUP_ID`, `TOKENROUTER_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`,
`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`) and throw a clear error naming the missing variable if
credentials for the selected provider are absent — this should fail loudly at
the call site, not silently return a canned reply (per the "no hidden fakes" rule).

## Vision-board input

`messages` must support either text content or ordered content parts:
`{ type: "text", text: string }` and `{ type: "image_url", imageUrl: string,
detail?: "low"|"high"|"auto" }`. Export `imageMessage(prompt, imageUrl)` for
the traits module. Preserve text-only callers. Map images to the
OpenAI-compatible `image_url` request shape; Anthropic accepts base64 image
data URLs and must clearly reject unsupported URL inputs.

# Dependencies
None — this is the base module everything else depends on.

# Acceptance criteria (see tests/llm.test.ts)
- `chatJSON` successfully parses a clean JSON response on the first try.
- `chatJSON` retries once and succeeds if the first response is JSON
  wrapped in markdown fences.
- `chatJSON` throws (does not silently return null/undefined) if both
  attempts fail to parse.
- Calling with an unset provider's API key throws a clear, named error
  rather than a generic fetch failure.
- TokenRouter sends a Chat Completions request to `api.tokenrouter.com` with
  a Bearer key, `messages`, and `max_tokens`, then returns
  `choices[0].message.content`.
- With `TOKENROUTER_MODEL` unset or set to legacy `"auto:balance"`, TokenRouter
  uses the verified `"google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite"` default.
- A Vision Board image becomes an OpenAI-compatible `image_url` content part.
